President Obama makes his first lightning visit to Florida and speaks at the Miami airport where he undertakes to improve air safety and integrity of US airspace. It also makes a quick two -day stop in the city of Orlando and meets with veterans who died in Vietnam and other conflicts before the return to Washington (October 11, 2011).

The US airlines, from last year, are being monitored by the TSA (Federal Government of Air Transport Security); Since then there have been many public protests in relation to this service.


